{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Like vinegar</b> — whose nature is cold and harms the teeth, or like smoke, whose nature is hot and harms the eyes — so the sluggard harms the interests of those who send him to do their work, and it is fitting for a person to separate from his company."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:58.838783227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}